{"type":"system","subtype":"background_tasks_changed","tasks":[{"task_id":"bqonybx4a","task_type":"local_bash","description":"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_2\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nPeople judge randomness by reading a sequence flip by flip with a gambler's-fallacy expectation: after each flip they expect the coin to \"balance out\" against the flips they have just seen, with recent flips weighing more than earlier ones (a fading memory), and a sequence looks random to the extent that its flips keep matching these balancing expectations (its probability under that self-correcting subjective coin). Because the expectation of a switch builds up the longer a streak continues, a long run is increasingly surprising beyond what its number of switches implies; people differ in how strongly they hold this balancing expectation.\nEOF\necho gamblers_fallacy_fading_memory > $D/model_name.txt\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/candidate.py\n\"\"\"Gambler's fallacy with fading memory (law-of-small-numbers subjective coin).\n\nPeople read a sequence flip by flip expecting the coin to balance out the\nflips they have just seen, recent flips weighing more (exponentially fading\nmemory). A sequence looks random to the extent its flips match these balancing\nexpectations, i.e. by its log-probability under that self-correcting subjective\ncoin. Expectation of a switch builds up as a streak continues, so long runs are\npenalised beyond their switch count. People differ in the strength of the\nbalancing expectation.\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport pymc as pm\nimport pytensor.tensor as pt\n\nL = 7  # max predicted positions (flips 2..8) and max lag\n\n\ndef _seq_feats(seq, tag):\n    seq = seq.strip().upper()\n    s = [1.0 if c == \"H\" else -1.0 for c in seq]\n    out = {}\n    for i in range(1, L + 1):\n        out[f\"m_{tag}_{i}\"] = 1.0 if i < len(s) else 0.0\n        for l in range(1, L + 1):\n            v = s[i] * s[i - l] if (i < len(s) and i - l >= 0) else 0.0\n            out[f\"p_{tag}_{i}_{l}\"] = v\n    return out\n\n\ndef compute_features(sequence_a, sequence_b):\n    f = _seq_feats(sequence_a, \"a\")\n    f.update(_seq_feats(sequence_b, \"b\"))\n    return f\n\n\ndef _score(tag, w_pow, g):\n    total = 0.0\n    for i in range(1, L + 1):\n        mask = pm.Data(f\"m_{tag}_{i}\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n        drive = 0.0\n        for l in range(1, i + 1):\n            prod = pm.Data(f\"p_{tag}_{i}_{l}\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n            drive = drive + w_pow[l - 1] * prod\n        for l in range(i + 1, L + 1):\n            # always zero, but bound so every feature key has a container\n            pm.Data(f\"p_{tag}_{i}_{l}\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n        # prod = s_i * s_{i-l}; a balancing expectation (g>0) makes a flip\n        # that repeats recent flips less probable.\n        total = total + mask * pt.log(pm.math.sigmoid(-g * drive))\n    return total\n\n\nwith pm.Model() as model:\n    participant_id = pm.Data(\"participant_id\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"int64\"))\n\n    # Person-specific strength of the balancing (gambler's fallacy) expectation.\n    g_mu = pm.Normal(\"g_mu\", mu=0.5, sigma=1.0)\n    g_sigma = pm.HalfNormal(\"g_sigma\", sigma=1.0)\n    g_z = pm.Normal(\"g_z\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=400)\n    g_person = g_mu + g_sigma * g_z\n    g = g_person[participant_id]\n\n    # Memory decay across lags (shared).\n    w = pm.Beta(\"w\", alpha=2.0, beta=2.0)\n    w_pow = [w ** k for k in range(L)]\n\n    # Choice sensitivity to the log-probability difference.\n    beta = pm.LogNormal(\"beta\", mu=0.0, sigma=0.75)\n\n    score_a = _score(\"a\", w_pow, g)\n    score_b = _score(\"b\", w_pow, g)\n\n    p_left = pm.Deterministic(\n        \"p_left\", pt.clip(pm.math.sigmoid(beta * (score_a - score_b)), 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n    )\n    chose_left = pm.Data(\"chose_left\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"int64\"))\n    pm.Bernoulli(\"response\", p=p_left, observed=chose_left)\nEOF\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run2/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -15"}],"uuid":"d027f703-a5a3-4b28-af7d-148d9ef9d7c6","session_id":"8d67a601-5366-4e01-b970-128795f72e9c"}
